          </div>
        </div>
      </header>

      <!-- ROUTE AT A GLANCE (CLICKABLE TO FILTER) -->
      <section class="section container">
        <div class="section-head">
          <div>
            <div class="section-kicker">Route at a glance · Tap a card to filter days</div>
            <h2>Save on beds &amp; transit.<br />Go all-in on experiences.</h2>
          </div>
          <p class="section-sub">
            Zero wasted backtracking: fly south for EDC Phuket, sweep overland through Krabi to Khao
            Sok Lake, sleep in the village to catch the 10:35 AM direct flight out of Surat Thani (URT) to
            Chiang Mai, and ride the CNR Overnight Sleeper Train back into Bangkok for New Year's Eve.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="route-grid">
          {
            routeBases.map((item) => (
              <article class="route-card" data-jump-city={item.cityKey}>
                <img src={item.image} alt={item.alt} loading="lazy" />
                <div class="route-card-body">
                  <div class="route-dates">{item.dates}</div>
                  <h3>{item.name}</h3>
                  <p>{item.summary}</p>
                  <div class="tag-row">
                    {item.tags.map((tag) => (
                      <span class="tag">{tag}</span>
                    ))}
                  </div>
                  <button type="button" class="route-filter-btn" data-jump-btn={item.cityKey}>
                    Filter {item.name} days ↓
                  </button>
                </div>
              </article>
            ))
          }
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- BUCKET LIST / UPGRADED HIGHLIGHTS -->
      <section id="highlights" class="section container">
        <div class="section-head">
          <div>
            <div class="section-kicker">Signature adrenaline &amp; bucket-list upgrades</div>
            <h2>The "unfiltered" moments<br />built into this route.</h2>
          </div>
          <p class="section-sub">
            Funded entirely by cutting Phuket surge taxis, dodging Thai ATM markups via SuperRich, flying direct
            from Surat Thani (URT) to Chiang Mai, and taking the CNR Sleeper Train.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="highlights-grid">
          <div class="highlight-box">
            <span class="hl-badge">Day 13 · Chiang Mai (Mae Rim)</span>
            <h3>🐅 Giant Tiger Shoulder Photos + 50m Bungee</h3>
            <p>
              Arrive at <strong>Tiger Kingdom Mae Rim at 9:00 AM sharp</strong> when cats are active. Trainers guide
              you to crouch right across a Giant Tiger's back/shoulders. Follow up with the <strong>Pongyang Jungle Coaster</strong>
              and <strong>50m Bungee Jump at X-Centre</strong>, getting back by 4:00 PM for the Sunday Walking Street.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="highlight-box">
            <span class="hl-badge">Day 14 · Mae Taeng Valley</span>
            <h3>🐘 Ethical Elephants + Bua Thong Sticky Waterfalls</h3>
            <p>
              Pairing the <strong>Ethical Elephant Sanctuary</strong> with <strong>Bua Thong Sticky Waterfalls</strong> in
              the same northern valley saves 2 hours of transit! Climb barefoot straight up mineral cascades, then hike
              the Monk's Trail to Wat Pha Lat for sunset chanting.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="highlight-box">
            <span class="hl-badge">Days 8–9 · Krabi &amp; Railay</span>
            <h3>✨ Glowing Plankton Night Swim &amp; Railay Climbing</h3>
            <p>
              Skip the crowded 9 AM boat for the <strong>7-Islands Sunset BBQ + Bioluminescent Plankton night snorkel</strong>,
              followed by a half-day <strong>top-rope limestone rock climb at Railay</strong> and secret Princess Lagoon scramble.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="highlight-box">
            <span class="hl-badge">Days 10 &amp; 19 · Khao Sok &amp; Bangkok</span>
            <h3>🥊 Cheow Lan Floating Bungalow &amp; Rajadamnern RWS</h3>
