        <div class="scam-rules-card">
          <h3>The 4 Golden Rules to Avoid Traps</h3>
          <ol class="scam-rules-list">
            <li>
              <strong>Never surrender your physical passport as a rental deposit:</strong> For motorbikes, jet skis, or equipment, reputable rental shops accept a clear photocopy of your passport photo page + a cash deposit (฿1,000–3,000). Handing over your original passport leaves you vulnerable to inflated extortion charges for preexisting scratches.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Never use camera flash inside tiger enclosures:</strong> At Tiger Kingdom Mae Rim, turn flash completely off and avoid sudden movements behind big cats. Always approach from behind under direct trainer guidance.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Book Sleeper Trains only on the official D-Ticket portal:</strong> Fake agency websites charge up to 50% markups on SRT Train #10 sleeper berths. Book directly at <a href="https://dticket.railway.co.th" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">dticket.railway.co.th</a>.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Exchange USD at SuperRich Basement B Floor to dodge ATM fees:</strong> Never withdraw multiple small amounts from Thai ATMs (each withdrawal charges ฿220 fee). Carry clean, crisp $100 USD bills from Dhaka and exchange them at SuperRich Thailand.
            </li>
          </ol>
        </div>
      </section>
